<BaseLayout lang="en" title="From Roll to Road: How Model-Specific Seat Covers Are Made | Livingstone" description="Digital cutting, computerized embroidery, 4-checkpoint QC — the process between your pattern file and a finished seat cover kit.">
  <section class="py-24 lg:py-32 px-6 bg-beige-50 min-h-screen">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/en/blog/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-charcoal-400 hover:text-sage-500 text-sm mb-10">← Back to Blog</a>
      <article class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-beige-200 p-8 md:p-12">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-charcoal-900 mb-3">From Roll to Road: How Model-Specific Seat Covers Are Made</h1>
        <p class="text-charcoal-400 text-sm mb-8">2026-10-04 · Jeff · 4 min read</p>
        <div class="text-charcoal-700 leading-relaxed space-y-5">
          <p>Most upholstery shops buy leather by the roll and do their own cutting. But for model-specific work — a full set for a 2022 Silverado, perforated inserts matched to OEM — there's a halfway option most shops never use: <b>pre-cut, pre-sewn kits made to your pattern</b>. Here's how that actually works in our factory.</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-charcoal-900 pt-2">Step 1 — Pattern in, spec locked</h2>
          <p>You send the pattern file or a template set. We confirm material (microfiber, PVC or genuine), thickness, color, perforation layout, and stitching style. Everything gets locked on a signed sample before production.</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-charcoal-900 pt-2">Step 2 — Digital cutting</h2>
          <p>Numerically-controlled cutting tables cut each panel to the pattern — headrests, bolsters, inserts, piping. No hand-tracing variance between unit 1 and unit 50.</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-charcoal-900 pt-2">Step 3 — Embroidery and perforation</h2>
          <p>Computerized embroidery handles logos (yours or the customer's). Digital perforation runs the exact hole pattern — diamond, vertical, OEM-spec — before any panel gets sewn.</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-charcoal-900 pt-2">Step 4 — Sewing, QC and packing</h2>
          <p>Sewing lines assemble the kit; QC checks stitching, color match and dimensions against the approved sample. Kits pack in moisture-protected wrapping with batch IDs, and out the door in 15–20 days for custom work.</p>
          <p>For shops, the math is simple: you skip cutting labor, reduce waste, and install faster. You keep the customer relationship — we stay your invisible factory.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-beige-200">
          <p class="text-charcoal-600 text-sm mb-4">We run this program for shops across the US — send us your pattern for a sample quote.</p>
